The generator builds on the theLook eCommerce dataset published by Looker
on the Google Cloud Marketplace (bigquery-public-data.thelook_ecommerce).
The files in src/data/ come from the upstream repository unchanged.

Changes made in this repository (Apache 2.0, section 4(b)):

- images/ (a demo GIF) was not copied.
- src/data/world_pop.csv is stored with LF line endings instead of CRLF
  (the repository's .gitattributes normalises all text files). The
  generator reads it in text mode, which accepts both.
- Dockerfile: base image pinned by version and digest; dependencies
  installed from requirements.lock (all versions pinned, with hashes)
  instead of the unpinned requirements.txt; runs as a non-root user;
  ENTRYPOINT fixed to generator.py (upstream ran data_generator.py, which
  does not exist).
- requirements.lock: added (generated with uv pip compile from
  requirements.txt, which is unchanged).
- Every change is visible in the Git history of this directory.
